abstract: "Modular PyTorch pipeline for studying backdoor preservation in federated unlearning: FedAvg simulation, dirty-label patch poisoning, retained-data fine-tuning, a corrected tensor-wise FedEraser, bounded gradient negation, Fine-Pruning, a paper-derived FedUP reimplementation, same-initialization counterfactual retraining and parameter-space alignment analysis, shipped with the experimental run records, provenance manifests and an executed reproduction notebook."
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - machine unlearning
  - backdoor attacks
  - reproducibility
